# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DataForSEO credentials
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Where to find them:
#   1. Go to https://app.dataforseo.com/api-access (sign up first if needed;
#      new accounts get $1 of free credit)
#   2. Click "Send by email"
#   3. DataForSEO emails you three values: "API login", "API password" and "Base64"
#
# Fill in ONE of the two options below. Leave the other option empty.
#
#   ┌──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┐
#   │ DataForSEO calls it  │ What it actually is      │ Goes in                  │
#   ├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
#   │ API login            │ Your account email       │ DATAFORSEO_EMAIL         │
#   │ API password         │ Your API key (NOT your   │ DATAFORSEO_API_KEY       │
#   │                      │ website password)        │                          │
#   │ Base64               │ Both of the above, in    │ DATAFORSEO_BASE64        │
#   │                      │ one string               │                          │
#   └──────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┘
#
# No quotes, no spaces around the "=". This file (as .env) is gitignored and
# never leaves your machine.

# ── Option A (recommended): your email + API key ────────────────────────────
DATAFORSEO_EMAIL=
DATAFORSEO_API_KEY=

# ── Option B: the Base64 value on its own ───────────────────────────────────
DATAFORSEO_BASE64=

# Filled in both options by accident? That's fine as long as they match;
# open-aso will tell you if they don't.
